The current trim_in_place only removes leading whitespace. I need to also remove trailing whitespace while preserving interior whitespace.

Let me fix it: after moving the start pointer forward, find the end of the string (after the memmove), and then trim trailing whitespace by null-terminating at the last non-space.

Let me write the fix.

Current code:
```c
void trim_in_place(char *value) {
    char *start = value;
    while (*start && isspace((unsigned char)*start)) start++;
    if (start != value) memmove(value, start, strlen(start) + 1);
}
```

I'll rewrite:

```c
#include <ctype.h>
#include <string.h>

void trim_in_place(char *value) {
    if (!value) return;
    char *start = value;
    while (*start && isspace((unsigned char)*start)) start++;
    if (start != value) memmove(value, start, strlen(start) + 1);

    size_t len = strlen(value);
    while (len > 0 && isspace((unsigned char)value[len - 1])) {
        value[--len] = '\0';
    }
}
```

This removes leading whitespace and trailing whitespace, preserving interior whitespace. Let me apply the patch and run the test.

